ies for engineering team of 6 developers\n   254→\n   255→      Business Analyst | Deloitte Consulting | Houston, TX | July 2017 - July 2019\n   256→      - Advised Fortune 500 clients on digital transformation strategy\n   257→      - Built financial models for technology investment decisions\n   258→      - Led requirements gathering workshops for enterprise software implementations\n   259→\n   260→      EDUCATION\n   261→\n   262→      MBA | McCombs School of Business, UT Austin | 2019\n   263→      - Concentration: Technology Commercialization\n   264→      - Product Management Club President\n   265→\n   266→      B.S. in Economics | Rice University | 2017\n   267→      - Minor: Computer Science\n   268→      - Cum Laude\n   269→\n   270→      SKILLS\n   271→\n   272→      Product: Roadmapping, user research, A/B testing, analytics, pricing strategy,\n   273→        go-to-market planning, competitive analysis\n   274→      Tools: Figma, Notion, Jira, Amplitude, Mixpanel, Looker, SQL, Python (basic),\n   275→        Miro, Dovetail\n   276→      Methodologies: Agile, Scrum, Jobs-to-be-Done, Design Thinking, OKRs\n   277→      Domain: B2B SaaS, collaboration tools, productivity software, developer tools\n   278→\n   279→      CERTIFICATIONS\n   280→      - Pragmatic Institute Certified Product Manager\n   281→      - Google Analytics Certified\n   282→      - Reforge Product Strategy Program (2023)\n   283→\n   284→      ACHIEVEMENTS\n   285→      - Product Hunt: #3 Product of the Day for Notion real-time features launch\n   286→      - Speaker at ProductCon Austin 2023: \"Building Products for the Async Workforce\"\n   287→      - Featured in First Round Review: \"How We Prioritize Features at Notion\"\n   288→\n   289→      INTERESTS\n   290→      - Angel investor in 3 early-stage B2B SaaS startups\n   291→      - Mentor at Austin Product Meetup\n   292→      - Avid rock climber and amateur coffee roaster\n   293→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file,